Description:

The cyrus-timezones package is now part of Cyrus: the IANA time zone database
is bundled in tzdata/, the guesstz library lives in imap/, and "make install"
generates and installs the VTIMEZONEs and the timezone guessing database that
were previously supplied by cyruslibs.

Along the way, "ctl_zoneinfo -r" fixes the zoneinfo index entry it writes for a
time zone alias that is a symlink in a region directory: Indian/Mayotte was
indexed as Mayotte, and so could not be resolved.

Documentation:

docsrc/download/installation/http/caldav.rst (TZDist chapter) and the new
cyr_guesstz(8) man page.

Config changes:

None.  zoneinfo_dir is unchanged, but now defaults to the directory the build
installed its time zone data into, rather than to nothing.

New configure options:

  --with-vzic=PATH        where to find the vzic timezone compiler
                          (default: search PATH; --without-vzic builds no
                          time zone data)

--without-guesstz is now a plain feature switch rather than a probe for an
external package, and no longer needs the guesstz.pc pkg-config file that
cyruslibs installed.

Upgrade instructions:

Nothing is required: an existing zoneinfo_dir setting still wins, and existing
time zone data keeps working.  The TZDist chapter of the documentation
describes how to hand over to the data Cyrus now installs.

Packagers: vzic is now a build-time dependency for the time zone data, and how
it was built matters -- see the same chapter.  Configure --without-vzic to keep
on shipping time zone data separately.

GitHub issue:

None.
